.TH AVR\-VM\-SSH 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-ssh \- Open an SSH session to a RUNNING VM, or run a command on it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm ssh
[OPTIONS] VM_ID [SSH_ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open an SSH session to a RUNNING VM, or run a command on it.
.PP
With no extra arguments this opens an interactive session. Anything after `--` is run as a remote command instead, e.g.:
.PP
avr vm ssh cvm-abc123 -- uname -a
.PP
A one-off `-- <cmd>` runs in a non-login shell that sources no startup files, so it won't see env forwarded by `avr vm bootstrap`. Pass `--login` to run it in a login shell instead (e.g. so `claude` finds its subscription token):
.PP
avr vm ssh cvm-abc123 --login -- claude -p 'summarize the repo'
.PP
Pass `--session <name>` to attach to (or create) a persistent tmux session, so the shell and any long-running process in it survive a dropped connection; reconnect with the same name to resume where you left off. A `-- <cmd>` given with --session runs only when the session is first created; reattaching to an existing session resumes it and does not rerun the command.
.PP
When the VM's endpoint publishes a host key it is pinned, so the first connect neither prompts nor is spoofable. If the endpoint has no host key, `avr` prints a warning and falls back to trust-on-first-use, so this spoofing protection is conditional rather than guaranteed. For port-forwarding use `avr vm port-forward`.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIVM_ID\fR
\&
.TP
[\fISSH_ARGS...\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIPATH\fR
Private key file to pass to ssh as -i.
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fITEXT\fR
Attach to (or create) a persistent tmux session by this name, so the shell and any long-running process in it survive a dropped connection. Reconnect with the same --session. A `-- <cmd>` runs only when the session is created, not on reattach.
.TP
\fB\-\-login\fR
Run the `-- <cmd>` in a login shell (bash -lc) so it sees bootstrap-forwarded env like CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN. Needed for a non-interactive command; a plain `ssh host cmd` shell sources nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the ssh command instead of running it.
